<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48149" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thērăsĭa</span></b> ,
		ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θηρασία,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small island in
				the Ægean Sea</i>, <i>opposite to
			Thea</i>, <i>westward</i>, <i>still
				called Therasia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 87, 89, § 202</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">4, 12, 23, §
			70</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 6, 21, 1</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>One of the Lipari islands near Sicily</i>, now <i>Vulcanello</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 9,
				14, § 93</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 6,
				§ 648</span></i>. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
